# RainNet hourly precipitation nowcasting benchmark

Code and result provenance for the paper *"Validation-isolated benchmarking
of hourly gridded precipitation nowcasting on the RainNet archive: classical,
deep, and verification-aware baselines"* (citation added upon publication).

A reproducible benchmark for hourly precipitation nowcasting built on the
RainNet dataset (Chen et al., NeurIPS 2022 Datasets & Benchmarks): given
10 past hourly frames, predict the next 10 hourly frames (+1h … +10h) over
the eastern United States on the low-resolution NLDAS product (208×333,
0.125° ≈ 13 km). Seven deep-model rows × 3 seeds are trained under one
protocol and compared with four classical rows (persistence, optical flow,
validation-tuned pysteps LK extrapolation and S-PROG), with a chronological test
year (2018) that is never used for selection, and a categorical and spatial
verification suite (CSI/POD/FAR/HSS at 0.1–10 mm rain-rate thresholds plus the
fractions skill score) alongside MSE/RMSE/MAE.

## Layout

```
docs/USER_GUIDE.md  installation, data, training, evaluation, and troubleshooting
docs/TUTORIAL.md  step-by-step run on the RainNet archive
examples/synthetic_demo.py  CPU-only evaluator demonstration; no RainNet download
examples/view_data_sample.py  per-frame statistics and panel for a data sample
data_samples/   five real 20-frame inspection windows (see data_samples/README.md)
corrected/     model + training code (the exact code that produced the paper
               numbers)
  model_nowcast.py            ConvLSTM family, ConvLSTM encoder-forecaster,
                              U-Net, SimVP v1, TAU, losses
  model_ConvLSTM.py           ConvLSTM cell
  main_nowcast_rainnet.py     training entry
  dataloader/dataloader_rainnet_fixed.py
  tools/train_function.py, tools/check.py
benchmark_tools/  data preparation + evaluation
  rainnet_build_lowres.py     stream-extract the lowres product (clip/140, fp16)
  rainnet_build_index.py      fixed window index (train 2002-2017 / test 2018)
  rainnet_build_index_blocked.py
                              month-blocked validation index for the
                              sensitivity analysis (seed 20261022; test split
                              copied unchanged; refuses to write on any
                              shared frame)
  rainnet_nowcast_eval.py     paper metrics (MSE/RMSE/MAE, CSI/POD/FAR/HSS);
                              writes strict JSON (undefined scores -> null)
  legacy/rainnet_nowcast_eval.e86540e9.py
                              the evaluator that wrote the pre-2026-10-22
                              eval JSONs (identical metrics; it wrote NaN
                              for undefined FAR, normalized to null in
                              results/eval_jsons/)
  tau_result_gate.py          accepts a TAU run only if it ended cleanly
                              (full run or explicit early stop) with finite
                              best-validation and test metrics
  tau_eval_waiter_20261022.sh       gated TAU test evaluation, one pass/seed
  rainnet_extended_eval.py     per-window metrics, FSS, sample dumps,
                              --split val (tuning-only carve)
  rainnet_pysteps_forecast.py pysteps baselines (LK extrapolation, S-PROG)
  pysteps_smoke_20261021.py   pysteps install/behaviour smoke test
  ext_eval_runner_20261021.sh       sequential eval of every benchmark row
  ext_eval_runner_20261022.sh       same, with the TAU result gate (added the
                                    three TAU rows; all other rows skipped)
  pysteps_tuning_20261021.sh        VALIDATION-only pysteps parameter tuning
local_checks/  tests + analysis
  test_nowcast_models.py      architecture/causality/param-count tests
  test_extended_eval.py       extended-evaluator tests (fake dataset)
  test_ext_analysis.py        bootstrap/FSS/CSI formula tests
  ext_analysis_paper1.py      day-block bootstrap CIs, paired tests, FSS,
                              heavy-rain CSI, train/val overlap disclosure
  make_figures_paper1.py      paper figures from the eval JSONs (+ pysteps npz)
  make_figures_paper1_v2.py   Figures 1-10 and E1 of the paper (maps, case
                              studies, per-window scatter, score curves)
  paper1_v2_derived_stats.py  test-year statistics, case-window selection
                              and per-window win rates (needs the archive)
  appendix_b_tables_paper1.py Appendix B tables from ext_summary.json
  test_tau_result_gate.py     TAU gate accept/reject cases
  test_eval_json_safety.py    strict-JSON serialization of undefined scores
  test_blocked_index.py       blocked-index builder and the loader's
                              explicit-'val' branch
results/       eval_jsons/ (24 strict-JSON outputs), analysis/ (EXT_ANALYSIS.md,
               ext_summary.json, Appendix B tables, pysteps validation-tuning
               summary and S-PROG grid), rainnet_index.json (the frozen split
               used in the paper), ext_eval/ (per-window metrics of every
               row, test-year observation statistics, and the forecast and
               observed fields of case windows 667 and 865), paper1_v2/
               (test-year statistics and maps from paper1_v2_derived_stats.py)
CHECKPOINTS.sha256   sha256 of every released checkpoint (Zenodo deposit)
MANIFEST.sha256      sha256 of every file in this tree
```

Note: `benchmark_tools/` was renamed from `queue_bundle/` for this release.
The former name is still the directory name on the compute server, so a few
comments and help strings inside the archived orchestration scripts refer to
`queue_bundle/`; those are historical references and no evaluation script
was modified. Every file under `corrected/` and `benchmark_tools/` is
byte-identical to the copy that produced the archived results (see
`MANIFEST.sha256`). `corrected/dataloader/dataloader_rainnet_fixed.py` and
`benchmark_tools/rainnet_extended_eval.py` are the versions that ran the
month-blocked rows. Each takes its new branch only when the index carries an
explicit `val` list; for `results/rainnet_index.json` both reproduce the
main-protocol windows bit-for-bit (checked by `test_blocked_index.py`).

To rebuild the month-blocked index (sha256 5e303b16… for the paper run):

```bash
python benchmark_tools/rainnet_build_index_blocked.py --lowres-dir data/rainnet/lowres \
  --source-index results/rainnet_index.json --out data/rainnet_blockval/rainnet_index.json
```

## Environment

Python 3.8–3.10 (3.10 recommended), then `pip install -r requirements.txt`. GPU optional: all
evaluation runs on CPU; training was done with torch 1.12.1 + CUDA 11.3 on
RTX 3090s. The pysteps baselines additionally need `pysteps==1.21.5` with
`opencv-python` (pinned: cv2 5.x requires numpy≥2 and breaks torch 1.12).

## Documentation

- [User guide](docs/USER_GUIDE.md)
- [Step-by-step tutorial](docs/TUTORIAL.md)
