  evaluator on toy data only and does not produce scientific results

## Data

0. Optional: inspect five real archive windows without the download
   (`data_samples/`, extracted by `benchmark_tools/extract_data_samples.py`).
1. Download `RainNet_HDF5.zip` (13.6 GB) from the official dataset repository:
   https://github.com/neuralchen/RainNet (Google Drive link in the README;
   dataset paper: Chen et al., NeurIPS 2022 Datasets & Benchmarks,
   arXiv:2012.09700; dataset distributed under CC BY).
2. Extract only the lowres product (fp16, one .npy per month, exactly the
   official recipe clip[0,140] mm then /140):
   `python benchmark_tools/rainnet_build_lowres.py --zip RainNet_HDF5.zip --out data/rainnet/lowres`
3. Build the window index (or copy `results/rainnet_index.json` for the
   byte-identical frozen split used in the paper):
   `python benchmark_tools/rainnet_build_index.py --lowres-dir data/rainnet/lowres --out data/rainnet/rainnet_index.json`
4. The loader additionally carves a disjoint 750-window validation set from
   the 6000 train windows with a fixed seed (`random.Random(2026)`); the
   1500-window 2018 test set is untouched by the carve and never used for
   selection.

## Training

```bash
python corrected/main_nowcast_rainnet.py --arch <convlstm_ed|unet|simvp|tau> \
  --loss <mse|balanced|tau_ddr> --data_path data/rainnet --batch_size 4 \
  --lr 1e-3 --lr_schedule cosine --num_epochs 50 --early_stop_patience 10 \
  --log_path logs/<name>.log --checkpoints checkpoints/<name>.pth
```

Protocol (identical for every benchmark row): 3 seeds (0/1/2), Adam,
cosine schedule from 1e-3, batch 4, ≤50 epochs, early stopping and
checkpoint selection on **validation MSE** — plain MSE also for
balanced-loss rows. The as-released ConvLSTM row keeps its family config
(batch 2, 20 epochs; see paper Section on the released configuration).

## Evaluation

```bash
# paper metrics (per-lead MSE/RMSE/MAE, CSI/POD/FAR/HSS at 0.1/0.5/1/2/5/10 mm)
python benchmark_tools/rainnet_nowcast_eval.py --data-path data/rainnet \
  --model simvp --checkpoints checkpoints/simvp_mse_rainnet_seed0.pth \
  --out results/eval_simvp_mse_rainnet_seed0.json

# extended per-window metrics (per-window MSE/MAE, contingency + FSS sums,
# deterministic sample dumps; identical accumulation order to the eval above)
python benchmark_tools/rainnet_extended_eval.py --data-path data/rainnet \
  --model simvp --checkpoints checkpoints/simvp_mse_rainnet_seed0.pth \
  --tag simvp_mse_rainnet_seed0 --out-dir artifacts/ext_eval

# pysteps baselines: parameters tuned on VALIDATION ONLY (never test) via
# benchmark_tools/pysteps_tuning_20261021.sh, then ONE test pass per method:
python benchmark_tools/rainnet_extended_eval.py --data-path data/rainnet \
  --model pysteps_sprog --pysteps-args '{"ar_order": 2, "n_cascade_levels": 8, "precip_thr": 0.1, "t_flow": 10}' \
  --tag pysteps_sprog --out-dir artifacts/ext_eval

# day-block bootstrap CIs, paired tests, FSS/heavy-rain tables, overlap audit
python local_checks/ext_analysis_paper1.py --ext-dir artifacts/ext_eval \
  --eval-dir results/eval_jsons --index-json results/rainnet_index.json

# figures (pysteps rows need their ext npz in --ext-dir; skipped otherwise)
python local_checks/make_figures_paper1.py --data-dir results/eval_jsons \
  --ext-dir artifacts/ext_eval --out-dir artifacts/figures

# Figures 1-10 and E1 of the paper, from the shipped files only
python local_checks/make_figures_paper1_v2.py --data-dir results/eval_jsons \
  --ext-dir results/ext_eval --v2-dir results/paper1_v2 \
  --out-dir artifacts/figures_v2
```

## Tests

Self-contained (small fake datasets are generated; no RainNet download needed):

```bash
python local_checks/test_nowcast_models.py    # architectures, causality, pinned param counts
python local_checks/test_extended_eval.py     # extended evaluator, FSS brute force, val carve
python local_checks/test_ext_analysis.py      # bootstrap/FSS/CSI formula tests
python local_checks/test_tau_result_gate.py   # TAU early-stop result gate
python local_checks/test_eval_json_safety.py  # strict JSON for undefined scores
```

Release copies of the tests differ from the originals only in release-layout
details: the default code-directory name (`corrected/`), the `benchmark_tools/`
path, and scratch output written to system temporary directories. The tested
behavior is unchanged.

## Results and provenance

- `results/eval_jsons/` — the strict-JSON outputs behind every paper number.
  Each records the model, checkpoint path, unit conversion, window count and
  observed data range. Files written before 2026-10-22 came from the legacy
  evaluator (included at `benchmark_tools/legacy/`; identical metrics, with
  NaN values normalized to null).
- `corrected/` and `benchmark_tools/` — byte-identical to the copies that
  produced the archived results. `MANIFEST.sha256` pins their checksums,
  e.g. `rainnet_nowcast_eval.py` (b9286227…) and
  `rainnet_extended_eval.py` (9d16b7de…).
- `CHECKPOINTS.sha256` — sha256 of every released checkpoint (shipped as a
  Zenodo deposit; not in the git tree).
- `MANIFEST.sha256` — sha256 of every file in this repository.

